Writer Duet provides a platform for screenwriting, scriptwriting and otherwriting projects. Multiple writers can work on the same document simultaneously.

Projects Section : Management of the overall project
Cards : it is used to separate scenes/sequences into cards
Comments : this are is used to recieve feedback
Analysis : This section is used to provide analysis of a script. There are different sections under thiis for different purposes such as formating, 
           break down the location, characters, provide grammar checking and any errors
Tools : Provides tools forr formating like underline, bold etc. It also allows writers to review or restore earlier versions. 
        Accept or reject the changes that has been made by a collaborator


Under each page there can be different sections. This is the element toolbar.It provides shortcuts for inserting different types of content into a screenplay. 
Each button represents a different script element.:
1) Scene : Creates a scene heading such as INT. HOUSE – NIGHT or EXT. STREET – DAY.
2) Action : Describes what is happening in the scene, including movements, events, and actions.
3) Characters : Adds a character name before their dialogue.
4) Parens : Adds a parenthetical instruction describing how a character says something or a small action during dialogue. Example: (whispering)
5) Dialogue : Add the words spoken by the character
6) Transition : Add a transition between 2 scenes like CUT TO, FADE OUT etc
7) Shot : Describes the shot type of the particular scene
8) Text : Adds general text that doesn't fit a standard screenplay element.
9) Note : Used to add a comment
10) Outline : Adds or manages outline information for organizing the story.
11) New Act : Marks the beginning of a new act in the screenplay.
12) End Act :	Marks the end of an act.
13) Lyrics : Used to enter song lyrics within the project.
14) Image : Inserts an image into the document.
15) Sequence : Creates or works with a sequence, which can contain a group of related scenes.
16) Dual : Creates dual dialogue, allowing two characters' dialogue to appear side-by-side, typically when they are speaking simultaneously.


there are also a lot of other features such as duplication of a project, exporting or importing a project, changing font such a styles, size, color etc. We ccan also 
add or remove collaborators to work on the same project.
